From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Bates <sbates@raithlin.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Nov 2026 10:12:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ionic: use the Rx buffer's page offset for XDP frags

ionic_run_xdp() describes every buffer after the first as a frag that
starts at offset 0 of its page, and syncs it for the CPU at the first
buffer's offset.  Since the Rx buffers come from page_pool_alloc(), a
buffer no larger than half a page is a page fragment and can start
anywhere in its page: the descriptor handed to the device has the right
address (ionic_rx_buf_pa() adds page_offset), the XDP frag does not.

With an MTU of 9000 the third buffer of a frame is 1402 bytes, so two of
them share a page and every second one starts at offset 1402.  An XDP
program then sees, and XDP_TX or XDP_REDIRECT sends, the start of the
page instead: the tail of whichever frame owns the other fragment, or
whatever the page held before if that fragment has not been filled yet.
That is an information leak onto the wire -- another frame's data, or
stale kernel memory, in a packet this host transmits.  The skb path is
not affected, it uses page_offset.

Found while testing XDP multi-buffer against the rocm-ernic userspace
emulated NIC, with a program that echoes 8000-byte UDP datagrams with
XDP_TX at MTU 9000: 5000 of 10000 echoes had their last 426 bytes
replaced by the bytes of another datagram.  With this patch all 10000
came back intact.

The same bug is in mainline.  This is not upstream yet; it has been
reported to the AMD Pensando team, who have not replied.  Drop this
patch once the fix lands in the kernel IONIC_KERNEL_REF pins.

Fixes: ac8813c0ab7d ("ionic: convert Rx queue buffers to use page_pool")
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_txrx.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_txrx.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_txrx.c
index e436e3231e86..16c2235e96da 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_txrx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_txrx.c
@@ -520,9 +520,9 @@ static bool ionic_run_xdp(struct ionic_rx_stats *stats,
 			bi++;
 			frag_len = min_t(u16, remain_len, bi->len);
 			page_pool_dma_sync_for_cpu(rxq->page_pool, bi->page,
-						   buf_info->page_offset,
-						   frag_len);
-			skb_frag_fill_page_desc(frag, bi->page, 0, frag_len);
+						   bi->page_offset, frag_len);
+			skb_frag_fill_page_desc(frag, bi->page,
+						bi->page_offset, frag_len);
 			sinfo->xdp_frags_size += frag_len;
 			remain_len -= frag_len;
 
